  factId: fact_twi_cold_coral
  habitatName: Cold-Water Lophelia Mound
  category: Deep-Sea Carbonate Bioherm
  zoneIndex: 1
  depthRangeText: "300\u2013700 m"
  habitatDescription: "An ancient carbonate bioherm built entirely in perpetual darkness
    by Lophelia pertusa and Madrepora corals in chilly 4\xB0C deep currents."
  ecologicalSignificance: Serves as deep-ocean biodiversity hotspots and breeding
    refuges for deep-water rockfish, squat lobsters, and fragile glass sponge gardens.
  interestingFact: Unlike shallow tropical corals, cold-water corals lack symbiotic
    photosynthetic algae (zooxanthellae) and filter 100% of sustenance from ocean
    currents.
  targetBiome: 2
  citationSource: NOAA Ocean Exploration / ATLAS Deep-Sea Project
